Commit:     Viche Executive <executive@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 8 10:04:00 2026 +0000

    government: treat a transient agent 'unknown' as non-fatal, not unhealthy
    
    Antonina intermittently reports state 'unknown' while a session transitions or
    recovers. Three executive-path sites treated one such sample as fatal:
    
    - appointments.sh ensure/resolve (mutations) exited 1 on any non-terminal state;
    - executive-cycle.sh aborted before dispatch with 'unexpected executive state';
    - branch-liveness.sh withheld the cycle and wrote readiness 'unhealthy'.
    
    The 09:58Z case executive_unhealthy:1794131744 is exactly this false positive.
    Each site now re-probes a bounded number of times (3, one second apart) and only
    then fails closed. Persistent unknown still withholds the cycle/branch and now
    reports a specific, actionable message ('re-probe', state, agent id) rather than
    an anonymous 'unexpected state'. No state is invented: a persistent unknown stays
    unhealthy; mutations still require a positively identified terminal state.
    
    tests/unknown-status-transient-smoke.sh proves both directions: a one-sample
    unknown still dispatches (rc=0) and yields readiness 'ready'; a persistent
    unknown dispatches nothing and exits 1. It fails on origin/main and passes here.

diff --git a/government/appointments.sh b/government/appointments.sh
index c6b85f5f..34a0fcf1 100644
--- a/government/appointments.sh
+++ b/government/appointments.sh
@@ -69,6 +69,19 @@ if [ -n "$old" ]; then
     exit 1
   fi
   status=$(printf '%s\n' "$meta" | jq -er '.state') || exit 1
+  # One "unknown" sample is a transient runtime observation, not a terminal
+  # state: re-probe a bounded number of times before deciding. A persistent
+  # unknown still fails closed for mutations below.
+  probe=0
+  while [ "$status" = unknown ] && [ "$probe" -lt 3 ]; do
+    probe=$((probe + 1))
+    sleep 1
+    if meta=$(antonina agent status --id "$old" --json 2>/dev/null); then
+      status=$(printf '%s\n' "$meta" | jq -er '.state' 2>/dev/null) || status=unknown
+    else
+      status=unknown
+    fi
+  done
   case "$status" in
     running|idle|clearexit) live=true;;
     failed|stopped|killed) :;;
@@ -79,7 +92,7 @@ if [ -n "$old" ]; then
       # sample breaks every caller (sitting, liveness, oversight). Mutations
       # still require a positively identified terminal state.
       if [ "$action" = resolve ]; then live=unknown
-      else echo "unknown status $status" >&2; exit 1
+      else echo "Viche: appointed agent $old still reports '$status' after $probe re-probe(s); refuse $action until a terminal state is proven" >&2; exit 1
       fi;;
   esac
 fi
